# Compact 152x72 Kessler surface compound. The larger atlas reservation remains untouched so
# future event staging, patrols, and the proving-ground fight have protected exterior space.
size 152 72
surface 54
entrance 61 42 3 10

# Clear only occupied architectural volumes. Natural terrain remains outside the compound and
# CorporateTerrainIntegration keys the foundation directly into the Wastes surface.
clear 4 13 20 43
clear 24 31 14 25
clear 38 5 76 51
clear 114 31 14 25
clear 128 13 20 43
clear 50 0 52 16

# Connected perimeter wall: paired checkpoint towers, overhead patrol walks, open ground-level
# passages, and terrain-anchored supports establish Kessler territory without a solid screen wall.
frame KesslerBlock 4 22 20 33 3
wall KesslerBulkheadWall 7 25 14 27
wall KesslerWindowWall 9 27 10 7
fill KesslerFloor 7 39 14 3
fill KesslerTrim 2 19 24 3
fill KesslerBeam 11 13 6 6
erase 4 44 3 8
erase 21 44 3 8
object KesslerLight 9 29 1 1
object KesslerLight 18 42 1 1

frame KesslerBlock 128 22 20 33 3
wall KesslerBulkheadWall 131 25 14 27
wall KesslerWindowWall 133 27 10 7
fill KesslerFloor 131 39 14 3
fill KesslerTrim 126 19 24 3
fill KesslerBeam 135 13 6 6
erase 128 44 3 8
erase 145 44 3 8
object KesslerLight 133 29 1 1
object KesslerLight 142 42 1 1

platform KesslerPlatform 24 37 14
platform KesslerPlatform 114 37 14
fill KesslerBeam 27 38 2 14
fill KesslerBeam 34 38 2 14
fill KesslerBeam 116 38 2 14
fill KesslerBeam 123 38 2 14

# Compact headquarters: a readable two-deck barracks and command block replaces the rejected
# oversized shell. Its stepped roof, inset glazing, beams, and crown use the validated native set.
frame KesslerBlock 38 16 76 39 3
wall KesslerBulkheadWall 41 19 70 33
wall KesslerWindowWall 44 21 16 8
wall KesslerWindowWall 68 21 16 8
wall KesslerWindowWall 92 21 16 8
fill KesslerFloor 41 34 70 3
fill KesslerFloor 41 52 70 3
fill KesslerBeam 61 37 3 15
fill KesslerBeam 88 37 3 15
fill KesslerTrim 36 13 80 3

frame KesslerBlock 54 8 44 11 2
wall KesslerWindowWall 56 10 40 7
fill KesslerTrim 50 5 52 3
fill KesslerBeam 73 0 6 5

# Public frontage: this west-side opening and quartermaster booth are accessible on day one.
# The separate internal bulkhead named by `entrance` remains sealed until Kessler arrives.
erase 38 43 3 9
fill KesslerGlass 61 42 3 10
object KesslerConsole 44 50 3 2
object KesslerTable 51 50 3 2
object KesslerChair 55 50 1 2 1
object KesslerLocker 58 49 2 3
object KesslerLight 45 41 1 1
object KesslerLight 57 41 1 1

# Lower armory and maintenance bays reserve the faction's future quartermaster inventory and
# provide immediate visual storytelling through animated armour, lockers, and service benches.
object KesslerPowerArmorRack 67 48 3 4
object KesslerPowerArmorRack 76 48 3 4
object KesslerConsole 82 50 3 2
object KesslerLocker 92 49 2 3
object KesslerWorkbench 97 51 2 1
object KesslerPowerArmorRack 104 48 3 4
object KesslerLight 70 40 1 1
object KesslerLight 83 40 1 1
object KesslerLight 97 40 1 1
object KesslerLight 108 40 1 1

# Upper command deck and standards make the compound identifiable from beyond the perimeter.
object KesslerConsole 44 32 3 2
object KesslerTable 53 32 3 2
object KesslerChair 51 32 1 2 0
object KesslerChair 57 32 1 2 1
object KesslerLocker 64 31 2 3
object KesslerConsole 73 32 3 2
object KesslerLocker 84 31 2 3
